# Student-facing rewrites of distractor rationales that the draft only stated as fragments. Keyed by (item id, fragment as extracted).
P={}
def a(i,frag,s): P[(i,frag)]=s
# 2.4
a("N-2.4-A","confuses an expected count with a guaranteed one.","This confuses an expected count (3% of 200 = 6) with a guaranteed count; the actual number in one shipment varies.")
a("N-2.4-A","confuses the event with its complement.","This confuses the event with its complement; 97% describes phones that are not defective and does not address the manager's claim of exactly 6.")
a("N-2.4-A","invents a minimum sample size; probability applies to each phone.","This invents a minimum shipment size; the 3% rate applies to every phone, so it applies to a shipment of 200.")
a("N-2.4-B","gave the complement (sum less than 4) and stopped.","This is P(sum < 4) = 3/36 = 1/12, the complement; the question asks for sums of at least 4, which is 1 − 1/12.")
a("N-2.4-B","counted sums of 4 or less as excluded (6 outcomes), i.e. computed P(sum > 4) = 30/36.","This counts a sum of 4 as excluded too (6 outcomes), so it finds P(sum > 4) = 30/36 = 5/6 instead of P(sum ≥ 4).")
a("N-2.4-B","treated sums above and below as equally likely.","This treats sums above and below the cutoff as equally likely, but the 36 outcomes are not split evenly.")
a("N-2.4-B-v1","counted sums of 5 as excluded (10 outcomes): 26/36.","This counts a sum of 5 as excluded too (10 outcomes), so it finds P(sum > 5) = 26/36 = 13/18 instead of P(sum ≥ 5).")
a("N-2.4-B-v2","both dice above 1, (5/6)².","This is the probability that both dice show more than 1, (5/6)² = 25/36; the question asks for at least one die above 1.")
a("N-2.4-B-v2","only one die considered.","This considers only one die; with two dice the chance that at least one is above 1 is higher.")
a("N-2.4-B-v3","used 3 flips.","This uses 3 flips (1 − 1/8) instead of the 4 flips in the question.")
a("N-2.4-B-v3","treated the 4 flips as 4 separate quarters (1 − 1/4).","This treats the four flips as one chance of 1/4 instead of multiplying the chances of four tails, (1/2)⁴ = 1/16.")
# 2.5
a("N-2.5-A","a union below 1 says nothing about overlap.","A union below 1 says nothing about whether the events overlap; here P(A and B) = 0.15 > 0, so they are not mutually exclusive.")
a("N-2.5-A","mutually exclusive events with positive probabilities can never be independent.","Mutually exclusive events with positive probabilities can never be independent, and these events are not mutually exclusive anyway because P(A and B) = 0.15.")
a("N-2.5-A","unequal sum shows overlap, not dependence.","P(A or B) ≠ P(A) + P(B) shows the events overlap, not that they are dependent; independence requires P(A and B) = P(A)P(B), which holds here.")
a("N-2.5-B","ignored the overlap (1 − 0.85).","This ignores the overlap: it adds 0.55 + 0.30 = 0.85 and takes 1 − 0.85, double counting students who take both.")
a("N-2.5-B","added the overlap instead of subtracting (1 − 0.95).","This adds the overlap (0.55 + 0.30 + 0.10 = 0.95) instead of subtracting it.")
a("N-2.5-B","only removed Spanish students (1 − 0.55).","This removes only the Spanish students (1 − 0.55) and forgets French students.")
a("N-2.5-A-v2","wrong inference from a sum under 1.","A sum of probabilities under 1 does not show that the events overlap; here P(A and B) = 0, so they are mutually exclusive.")
a("N-2.5-A-v2","the common \"they cannot affect each other\" confusion.","This confuses mutually exclusive with independent; mutually exclusive events with positive probabilities strongly affect each other, because one happening rules out the other.")
a("N-2.5-B-v1","ignored the overlap (1 − 0.70).","This ignores the overlap: it adds 0.45 + 0.25 = 0.70 and takes 1 − 0.70.")
a("N-2.5-B-v1","only removed bikers (1 − 0.45).","This removes only the commuters who bike (1 − 0.45) and forgets those who take the bus.")
a("N-2.5-B-v1","added the overlap (1 − 0.80).","This adds the overlap (0.45 + 0.25 + 0.10 = 0.80) instead of subtracting it.")
a("N-2.5-B-v2","ignored the overlap (1 − 0.65).","This ignores the overlap: it adds 0.38 + 0.27 = 0.65 and takes 1 − 0.65.")
a("N-2.5-B-v2","added the overlap (1 − 0.74).","This adds the overlap (0.38 + 0.27 + 0.09 = 0.74) instead of subtracting it.")
a("N-2.5-B-v2","only removed online readers.","This removes only the online readers (1 − 0.38) and forgets the print readers.")
a("N-2.5-B-v3","ignored the overlap (1 − 160/200).","This ignores the overlap: it adds 90 + 70 = 160 students and takes 1 − 160/200.")
a("N-2.5-B-v3","added the overlap (1 − 190/200).","This adds the overlap (90 + 70 + 30 = 190) instead of subtracting it.")
