a("N-2.12-B-v1","unchanged.","The standard deviation of the sample mean is σ/√n, so it changes when n changes.")
a("N-2.12-B-v1","increased.","Larger samples give less variable sample means, so the standard deviation decreases rather than increases.")
a("N-2.12-B-v2","increased.","Larger samples give less variable sample means, so the standard deviation decreases rather than increases.")
a("N-2.12-B-v2","divided by 4 again (÷4).","The standard deviation depends on √n, so quadrupling n halves it; it does not divide it by 4.")
a("N-2.12-B-v3","forgot the square root.","This forgets the square root: multiplying n by 3 divides the standard deviation by √3, not by 3.")
a("N-2.12-B-v3","cubed.","This multiplies n by 27, which divides the standard deviation by √27 ≈ 5.2, not by 3.")
a("N-2.3-A-v1",'"none in three" estimates "at least 4 tickets".','Recording "no winner in three tickets" estimates the chance of needing at least 4 tickets, not at least 3.')
